WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:03.249
Film Courage: Gordy we had a question come
in earlier from Twitter, it’s a lady named

00:00:03.249 --> 00:00:08.290
Mexie and she’s from Australia I believe
and she says I would love to see interviews

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.780
or discussions on developing secondary characters.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.549
So any thoughts on developing secondary characters?

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:17.990
Gordy Hoffman, Founder/Judge of BlueCat Screenplay
Competition: Well your cast size is always

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:26.199
a concern because you have to give each character
enough real estate in your script to create

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:32.119
enough moments (emotional moments) that the
audience can relate to and identify and connect

00:00:32.119 --> 00:00:39.900
with and secondary, primary, supporting, if
you choose to have a character that you are

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:45.280
going to develop, you can arc them out in
the same way like what is the beginning, middle

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.870
and end of this journey of this character.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:52.359
I wouldn’t get too concerned with theme
or how they relate or whatever but if you’re

00:00:52.359 --> 00:00:57.860
trying to develop any character, you want
to be like well what is there, do you have

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:03.160
enough scenes where the audience can relate
and are they going on an emotional journey,

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:10.780
an interior journey, an external journey (whatever),
the combination of both.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:17.100
But you build it the same way of any of your
characters.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:25.659
You want to create enough moments where the
audience can see themselves so it’s plausible,

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:31.869
emotional, high stakes stuff where the audience
can see themselves reflected and they identify

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:33.630
and they sympathize.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:38.860
So it’s the same things, that’s how I
look at everything.

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:46.710
I don’t get caught up in like formulas as
to where things are suppose to happen in stories.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:52.310
I think it’s mostly you want to focus on
you know and I don’t think there’s a lot

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:59.880
talked about with character so it’s a very
good question but mostly it’s the screenplay

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.119
only has so long.

00:02:01.119 --> 00:02:05.549
You only have two to two and a half hours
to go right or something like that (an hour

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:10.940
and a half) and you want to have as many moments
because a relationship is defined by the volume

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.890
of moments that we have with the person.

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:18.540
If you have coffee with the person once a
year then if you pass away you have one kind

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.580
of emotional response.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:24.070
If you have coffee with somebody everyday
out of the whole year that’s going to hit

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:25.250
you more.

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:30.030
So in the script if we see that secondary
character or any character and we’re able

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:35.870
to see them different context go through different
things and there is a greater volume of access

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:42.200
to them in different days, different times,
different locations, doing different things

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:48.190
and bouncing through this plot that’s why
cast sizes are small that’s why with CASABLANCA

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:50.350
it’s basically a story about three people.

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:55.790
That’s why Harry Potter’s eight movies
basically around three people (really around

00:02:55.790 --> 00:03:02.740
one guy), there’s three people, I mean there’s
other characters but we’re not asked to

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:04.980
connect with a bunch.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:09.350
When you have something longer like GAME OF
THRONES you’re able to connect with more

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:13.750
people because there’s more real estate
but that’s only because there’s more real

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:19.380
estate and that’s how we find our way in
to the main characters but still there are

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:46.650
a few that garner most of our attention.

